{"id":"feedback-bd-cpp-standard-scope-001","question":"How do I run a normal first Black Duck SCA scan using the Black Duck C/C++ tool? Assume BD_HUB_TOKEN is already set in my environment. Show a shell-neutral CLI command that includes my actual build command without assuming a build system.","product":"blackduck-sca","product_version":"latest","expected_behavior":"answer","must_retrieve":["BlackDuck SCA/docs/c-cpp-tool/black-duck-c-cpp-tool/executing-the-black-duck-c-cpp-tool.md"],"should_retrieve":["BlackDuck SCA/docs/c-cpp-tool/black-duck-c-cpp-tool/frequently-asked-questions.md"],"must_not_retrieve":[],"required_facts":[{"type":"EXACT_FACT","value":"blackduck-c-cpp","case_sensitive":true},{"type":"EXACT_FACT","value":"--build_cmd","case_sensitive":true},{"type":"EXACT_FACT","value":"--build_dir","case_sensitive":true},{"type":"EXACT_FACT","value":"--project_name","case_sensitive":true},{"type":"EXACT_FACT","value":"--project_version","case_sensitive":true},{"type":"EXACT_FACT","value":"--bd_url","case_sensitive":true},{"type":"EXACT_FACT","value":"--api_token","case_sensitive":true}],"forbidden_facts":[{"type":"EXACT_FACT","value":"--additional_sig_scan_args","case_sensitive":true},{"type":"EXACT_FACT","value":"--snippet-matching","case_sensitive":true}],"source_evidence":[{"file":"BlackDuck SCA/docs/c-cpp-tool/black-duck-c-cpp-tool/executing-the-black-duck-c-cpp-tool.md","section":"## Command line options","corpus_revision":"bd-docs-9485d952-20260823"},{"file":"BlackDuck SCA/docs/c-cpp-tool/black-duck-c-cpp-tool/frequently-asked-questions.md","section":"20. **I already have run Black Duck C/CPP once.","corpus_revision":"bd-docs-9485d952-20260823"}],"verification_status":"verified","verified_by":"user-feedback+deterministic-corpus-check","origin":"team-feedback","runtime_classification":"DOC_ONLY","notes":"For a normal first scan, include the customer's actual build command to capture build data; do not assume make. The option table labels build_cmd optional because prior build data can be reused with skip_build. The FAQ documents offline-file reuse with use_offline_files plus skip_build, and also skip_build after a completed build with later errors. Accept documented short or long options and BD_HUB_TOKEN in place of a command-line token."}
{"id":"feedback-sca-project-definition-001","question":"Explain what a Black Duck SCA project is to a new customer who is unfamiliar with the product.","product":"blackduck-sca","product_version":"2026.7","expected_behavior":"answer","must_retrieve":[],"should_retrieve":["BlackDuck SCA/docs/help-center/understanding-projects-in-black-duck/about-project-versions/creating-a-new-version-of-a-project.md"],"must_not_retrieve":[],"required_facts":[{"type":"EXACT_FACT","value":"stand-alone development project"},{"type":"EXACT_FACT","value":"part of another project"},{"type":"EXACT_FACT","value":"project version"}],"forbidden_facts":[],"source_evidence":[{"file":"BlackDuck SCA/docs/help-center/getting-started-with-black-duck-sca.md","section":"# Getting started with Black Duck SCA","corpus_revision":"bd-docs-9485d952-20260823"},{"file":"BlackDuck SCA/docs/help-center/understanding-projects-in-black-duck/about-project-versions/creating-a-new-version-of-a-project.md","section":"# Creating a new version of a project","corpus_revision":"bd-docs-9485d952-20260823"},{"file":"BlackDuck SCA/docs/help-center/understanding-projects-in-black-duck/creating-a-project.md","section":"# Creating a project","corpus_revision":"blackduck-2026.7"}],"verification_status":"verified","verified_by":"Tony+deterministic-corpus-check","origin":"team-feedback","runtime_classification":"DOC_ONLY","notes":"DS-07 benchmark revision accepts either version-matched page that contains the same project definition. Promoted from sca-project-001 human review. Guards against repeating the vague phrase base unit without explaining the project/version relationship for a new customer. The literal phrase base unit is not required when the answer explains the relationship.","must_retrieve_any":["BlackDuck SCA/docs/help-center/understanding-projects-in-black-duck/creating-a-project.md","BlackDuck SCA/docs/help-center/getting-started-with-black-duck-sca.md"]}
{"id":"feedback-sca-phase-selection-001","question":"A new Black Duck SCA 2026.7 project version is in active development, not planning or released. Which Phase should I select, and why?","product":"blackduck-sca","product_version":"2026.7","expected_behavior":"answer","must_retrieve":["BlackDuck SCA/docs/help-center/understanding-projects-in-black-duck/about-project-versions/about-project-version-phases.md"],"should_retrieve":["BlackDuck SCA/docs/help-center/understanding-projects-in-black-duck/about-project-versions/creating-a-new-version-of-a-project.md"],"must_not_retrieve":[],"required_facts":[{"type":"EXACT_FACT","value":"In Development"}],"forbidden_facts":[{"type":"EXACT_FACT","value":"In Planning is always the correct phase"}],"source_evidence":[{"file":"BlackDuck SCA/docs/help-center/understanding-projects-in-black-duck/about-project-versions/about-project-version-phases.md","section":"# About project version phases","corpus_revision":"bd-docs-9485d952-20260823"}],"verification_status":"verified","verified_by":"Tony+deterministic-corpus-check","origin":"team-feedback","runtime_classification":"DOC_ONLY","notes":"Scenario-based reference case. Select In Development for work in progress; In Planning is only the default. Review the reason against the current lifecycle stage."}
{"id":"feedback-sca-distribution-selection-001","question":"My Black Duck SCA 2026.7 project version is a hosted SaaS product. Customers use the service but do not receive the software. Which Distribution should I select, and why?","product":"blackduck-sca","product_version":"2026.7","expected_behavior":"answer","must_retrieve":["BlackDuck SCA/docs/help-center/understanding-projects-in-black-duck/about-project-versions/creating-a-new-version-of-a-project.md"],"should_retrieve":[],"must_not_retrieve":[],"required_facts":[{"type":"EXACT_FACT","value":"SaaS"},{"type":"EXACT_FACT","value":"hosted"}],"forbidden_facts":[{"type":"EXACT_FACT","value":"External is always the correct distribution"}],"source_evidence":[{"file":"BlackDuck SCA/docs/help-center/understanding-projects-in-black-duck/about-project-versions/creating-a-new-version-of-a-project.md","section":"# Creating a new version of a project","corpus_revision":"bd-docs-9485d952-20260823"}],"verification_status":"verified","verified_by":"Tony+deterministic-corpus-check","origin":"team-feedback","runtime_classification":"DOC_ONLY","notes":"Scenario-based routine case. A hosted-only service uses SaaS; External is the default, not a universal recommendation. Review the reason, not only the option label."}
